        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(android): add inline dictation to chat composer",
        "body": "[AI-assisted]\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nAndroid Chat’s attachment, voice-note, dictation, and realtime Talk controls compete for space around the message field. Separate microphone actions make the composer feel cramped, while starting realtime Talk can leave the active Chat surface and send users without a configured provider directly to Settings.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis update consolidates the controls into one rounded composer: attachment on the left, editable text in the center, one microphone for tap-to-dictate and long-press voice-note capture, and realtime Talk on the right. Send reuses the Talk slot when a draft is sendable. Realtime Talk now reuses the existing Talk runtime as a composer state: the same red button starts the session, animates while live, and stops it on the next tap without replacing Chat. Missing-provider readiness is reported in place without automatic navigation, and legacy Voice routes normalize back to Chat without adding a second audio or session stack.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAndroid users get one coherent Chat surface: + adds attachments, tapping the mic inserts dictated text, holding it starts a voice note with haptic feedback, and the red Talk button starts realtime Talk. While live, that same button shows an animated waveform and remains the stop control even when the draft contains text; while idle, a sendable draft swaps the slot to Send. No Talk page, dock, or setup card replaces Chat, and missing-provider readiness appears as a short message without navigating away.\n\n## Evidence\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> ### Validation\n>\n> - [x] `git diff --check` — passed on the combined head after merging the latest origin/main\n> - [x] `pnpm native:i18n:sync` — passed with entries=4829 and changed=false after the final i18n inventory alignment\n> - [x] `pnpm native:i18n:check` — passed; repository advisories remained non-blocking\n> - [x] `pnpm android:i18n:check` — passed\n> - [x] `pnpm apple:i18n:check` — passed\n> - [x] `./gradlew --no-daemon :app:testPlayDebugUnitTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.ui.chat.ChatDictationControllerTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.ui.chat.ChatComposerDraftTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.VoiceWakeRuntimeTest` — focused composer and dictation tests passed\n> - [x] `node scripts/run-android-gradle.mjs :app:testPlayDebugUnitTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.ui.ShellScreenLogicTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.ui.chat.ChatScreenTest` — focused navigation and inline Talk tests passed after merging the latest origin/main\n> - [x] `pnpm android:assemble` — completed successfully on the final combined origin/main-based head\n> - [x] `./gradlew :app:testPlayDebugUnitTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.ui.chat.ChatScreenTest` — passed on the final physical-proof head\n> - [x] `./gradlew :app:ktlintCheck :app:assemblePlayDebug` — passed on the final physical-proof head\n> - [x] `adb install -r` — installed the scoped patched APKs successfully; installation readback matched the built artifacts byte-for-byte\n\n> [!TIP]\n> ### Real Behavior Proof\n>\n> Final runtime behavior was verified on a physical Android device using exact runtime head `b8b2c92d17aac0902553bdb560a1adb5534ae9d6`. Current PR head `b959d97e0328acbb36510e2e5d51c2d962b4735c` contains only the follow-up i18n inventory alignment and removal of non-user-visible Compose tooling labels; dictation and Talk runtime behavior are unchanged.\n>\n> - [x] **Environment:** Physical Android device at 720x1600 with font scale 1.0; the final runtime APK was installed with state-retaining `adb install -r`.\n> - [x] **Precondition:** Chat, its active conversation, and the message input remained visible.\n> - [x] **Inline dictation:** The recording taps the composer microphone, completes speech recognition, and visibly inserts the final recognized text into the unsent Chat input field (the “active Chat draft” in review terminology).\n> - [x] **Embedded Talk:** The same red composer button starts Talk, animates as a waveform while live, and stops Talk on the next tap; Chat, the conversation, and the composer remain visible.\n> - [x] **Result:** Both dictation-to-input and Talk-in-Chat are shown without a Talk page, dock, setup card, or automatic Settings navigation replacing the active Chat surface.\n\n### Final physical behavior proof — inline dictation and embedded Talk\n\nPhysical device — exact runtime head `b8b2c92d17aac0902553bdb560a1adb5534ae9d6`, behavior-identical to current head `b959d97e0328acbb36510e2e5d51c2d962b4735c`: this single recording shows the mic-tap recognition result appearing in the unsent Chat input field, followed by realtime Talk starting, showing the live waveform, and stopping from the same composer while the active Chat remains visible.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1b72f70b-142f-46c0-881f-35e83750c53d\n\n### Composer layout\n\n<table>\n  <tr><th>Before</th><th>After</th></tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><img width=\"260\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f4e5c78b-c386-4aa6-96d5-eb6867fc1090\" alt=\"Composer before\" /></td>\n    <td><img width=\"260\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dda525bc-9a49-46bf-8bb5-6ace01daa8ca\" alt=\"Composer after\" /></td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\nAdditional composer behavior recording — mic tap inserts recognized text into the unsent Chat input field; long-press remains the separate voice-note gesture:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8c6119b0-a68c-426b-b13e-573af98e07a9\n\n### Earlier realtime Talk iteration\n\n<table>\n  <tr><th>Before</th><th>After</th></tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><img width=\"260\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/48548519-30aa-4de9-ad62-53a94294a868\" alt=\"Realtime Talk before\" /></td>\n    <td><img width=\"260\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6ef75626-9e79-4b37-be21-203885727f84\" alt=\"Realtime Talk after\" /></td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\nBefore realtime Talk behavior recording:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6c483090-d99f-479a-b5f4-8af4e97c92f1\n\nAfter realtime Talk behavior recording:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d92cc8e2-ffef-4823-ab05-3a8cde0067d3\n",
